WEBVTT

00:02.450 --> 00:05.820
Well then, now that Reinhard
and the others are here,

00:05.820 --> 00:08.950
we should discuss
the Witch Cult's four demands.

00:08.950 --> 00:09.910
Yes.

00:10.280 --> 00:15.450
We know of the silver-haired maiden,
Witch's bones, and the artificial spirit.

00:15.450 --> 00:18.040
Yeah. The spirit they want
is Beatrice, right?

00:18.040 --> 00:20.380
Yes. But the Book of Wisdom, however...

00:20.380 --> 00:22.040
The Book of Wisdom, you say?

00:22.040 --> 00:24.210
Does it even exist?

00:24.210 --> 00:26.590
Sorry, about the Book of Wisdom...

00:27.140 --> 00:30.010
I actually brought one into this city.

00:30.760 --> 00:35.010
What?!

00:36.980 --> 00:39.850
Why the heck do you have
a Book of Wisdom?!

00:40.230 --> 00:41.770
Let's save that for later.

00:41.770 --> 00:46.860
The Book of Wisdom is apparently
the origin of the Witch Cult's Gospel.

00:47.300 --> 00:48.740
Its origin, you say?

00:48.740 --> 00:52.240
It's no wonder why they want it, then.

00:52.240 --> 00:53.280
Yes.

00:53.280 --> 00:56.160
However, by the time I got it,

00:56.160 --> 00:59.330
it was just a pile of unreadable
charred scraps,

00:59.330 --> 01:02.330
so I left it at a restorer,
hoping they could fix it.

01:02.330 --> 01:05.460
They can fix it in that state?
Is that even possible?

01:05.460 --> 01:06.680
Then...

01:07.920 --> 01:10.050
When we split up yesterday, you were...

01:10.050 --> 01:11.130
Yes, that's right.

01:11.580 --> 01:12.840
Anyway,

01:12.840 --> 01:16.970
I'll skip over how I got it
and what I'll do with it once it's restored.

01:16.970 --> 01:19.900
Anything more is an internal matter.

01:19.900 --> 01:22.270
I won't pry into the specifics,

01:22.270 --> 01:25.480
but it's clear we've got everythin'
the Witch Cult's lookin' for.

01:25.480 --> 01:29.070
That said, we can't let any of them
fall into their hands.

01:29.420 --> 01:31.360
That's our decision, right?

01:31.360 --> 01:33.110
Still, I've gotta say...

01:33.110 --> 01:38.120
Most of what they want
is from yer camp, pal.

01:38.120 --> 01:41.210
Oh, come on.
You don't have to tell me that.

01:42.470 --> 01:43.500
I've had a revelation!

01:43.860 --> 01:44.830
Please listen:

01:44.830 --> 01:47.250
Mad 'n Crazy About Every Bit of You!

01:47.250 --> 01:47.850
Liliana?!

01:47.850 --> 01:48.300
♪ I'm mad 'n crazy about you, ♪

01:48.300 --> 01:49.880
♪ I'm mad 'n crazy about you, ♪
That means...

01:49.880 --> 01:50.760
♪ but I'm running around in circles ♪

01:50.760 --> 01:54.140
♪ but I'm running around in circles ♪
What else could it mean but me personally

01:54.140 --> 01:56.350
♪ What should I do? ♪
gracing your presence, peasant?

01:56.350 --> 01:57.810
♪ I just can't stop loving you ♪
P-Princess!

01:57.810 --> 01:59.220
♪ I just can't stop loving you ♪
You're okay!

01:59.220 --> 02:00.100
♪ I'm always madly crazy about you, and yet— ♪
I was so wor—

02:00.100 --> 02:01.890
♪ I'm always madly crazy about you, and yet— ♪

02:03.140 --> 02:05.480
Ack! My elbows! My knees!

02:05.480 --> 02:08.360
The pain of every bone
in my body breaking!

02:08.360 --> 02:10.690
All my six ribs just gave in!

02:10.690 --> 02:17.780
Al, how dare you fool around with commoners
without attending to my needs?

02:17.780 --> 02:22.460
And you, Schult, even had the audacity
to make me personally search for you.

02:22.460 --> 02:26.960
Ugh, my humblest apologies,
Lady Priscilla, ma'am...

02:26.960 --> 02:29.670
You actually followed through.

02:29.670 --> 02:31.840
You really are competent.

02:31.840 --> 02:34.550
That clumsy broadcast earlier...

02:34.550 --> 02:36.680
That was your voice, was it not?

02:37.070 --> 02:38.390
And what if it was?

02:38.390 --> 02:40.800
Hah! Do not be so tense.

02:40.800 --> 02:43.350
I am always fair
when it comes to results.

02:43.830 --> 02:46.900
As a reward,
I shall join in on your scheme.

02:46.900 --> 02:48.770
You should feel honored.

02:48.770 --> 02:50.980
Wait, Princess!

02:50.980 --> 02:54.570
Are you seriously gonna
take on the Witch Cult?

02:54.570 --> 02:58.280
Would you have me flee, Al?

02:58.730 --> 03:02.040
You'd best remember
that even insolence has its limits.

03:02.700 --> 03:06.210
Now, explain the situation to me.

03:06.210 --> 03:09.750
- Alright, Princess. I got it, okay?
- Otto, can we talk outside for a bit?

03:10.290 --> 03:11.630
It was a year ago.

03:12.210 --> 03:16.090
I collected the burnt remnants
of the Book of Wisdom in the Sanctuary.

03:16.090 --> 03:18.760
So, it's Roswaal's book, then?

03:18.760 --> 03:20.140
Yes.

03:20.140 --> 03:23.530
It's also the one I wanted to verify.

03:24.850 --> 03:28.940
I have absolutely no trust
in Margrave Mathers.

03:29.690 --> 03:31.560
Sure, there was the Sanctuary,

03:31.560 --> 03:35.650
but his schemes go back
much further than that.

03:35.650 --> 03:38.700
I feel like everyone
forgave him too easily.

03:39.190 --> 03:41.620
I haven't completely forgiven him.

03:41.620 --> 03:44.830
But that doesn't change
the fact that we need him.

03:45.280 --> 03:46.160
That's why...

03:47.210 --> 03:48.420
And that's okay.

03:48.420 --> 03:51.840
You and Lady Emilia are fine like that,

03:51.840 --> 03:55.380
since I'll be there to keep watch
when you're not looking.

03:55.380 --> 03:57.550
Keep watch while we're...?

03:57.980 --> 03:59.470
As the domestic adviser,

03:59.470 --> 04:03.010
I've had many opportunities to interact
with him over the past year.

04:03.590 --> 04:08.100
From what I've observed, I didn't pick up
on any schemes or ill intentions.

04:08.480 --> 04:11.860
But what if he has some sort of
pre-arranged scheme in motion?

04:12.400 --> 04:16.650
If he's still following that book,
then all his plans are written there.

04:16.650 --> 04:20.240
That would definitely be
beneficial in the future.

04:20.240 --> 04:21.570
That's why you...

04:21.940 --> 04:26.580
I wanted to make sure that no one
in our faction was going to get hurt.

04:26.580 --> 04:29.420
That's why I sent the Book of Wisdom
for restoration.

04:29.420 --> 04:32.390
I'm sorry for my selfish actions.

04:34.520 --> 04:37.720
Alright, I get why you did what you did.

04:38.200 --> 04:42.300
Problem is, what are we going
to do about that book?

04:42.300 --> 04:44.470
Retrieving it is my responsibility.

04:44.890 --> 04:47.350
Taking back the towers
is our top priority.

04:47.350 --> 04:49.310
We can't send in anyone to help you.

04:49.310 --> 04:51.230
I survived this dangerous city

04:51.230 --> 04:54.900
and even brought the Sword Saint
along with me, remember?

04:57.440 --> 05:00.360
Right. Don't screw up now, alright?

05:00.760 --> 05:01.740
Right.

05:01.740 --> 05:02.910
Sir Subaru.

05:02.910 --> 05:04.160
Mr. Wilhelm!

05:04.160 --> 05:07.290
My apologies for not joining the meeting.

05:07.290 --> 05:08.660
You don't have to...

05:08.660 --> 05:10.290
More importantly, how's Ms. Crusch?

05:10.700 --> 05:12.830
She opened her eyes just moments ago.

05:12.830 --> 05:18.510
Though her condition is still delicate,
she asked me to call for you.

05:18.950 --> 05:19.960
Me?

05:24.800 --> 05:26.490
Subawu...

05:27.890 --> 05:30.770
Don't you dare make her push herself.

05:30.770 --> 05:32.020
Right...

05:41.030 --> 05:43.910
...aster... Su... baru...?

05:45.490 --> 05:50.910
...I apologize...
for the unpleasant sight...

05:51.320 --> 05:54.380
No... you don't have to... apologize...

05:54.840 --> 05:58.710
Is this... really the same
dragon blood curse as I have?

06:00.880 --> 06:01.760
Ferris!

06:06.300 --> 06:09.460
Ms. Crusch...
is there something I can help with?

06:10.180 --> 06:12.810
Thank goodness... you're safe...

06:14.520 --> 06:20.480
I heard... you were exposed
to the blood... like I was...

06:20.880 --> 06:22.900
I'm fine. Don't worry about me.

06:22.900 --> 06:24.700
You're the one—

06:27.740 --> 06:28.780
What...?

06:29.660 --> 06:30.950
Show it to me.

06:38.750 --> 06:39.630
Ferris!

06:40.170 --> 06:41.590
Ms. Crusch's hand!

06:42.340 --> 06:46.220
Did it shift from her body to mine?!

06:46.220 --> 06:49.680
But nothing happens when I touch her!

06:52.060 --> 06:53.770
See? Nothing's happening!

06:53.770 --> 06:55.060
I...

06:55.060 --> 06:59.110
Why can't I even help her
at a time like this!?

06:59.530 --> 07:00.690
Move, Ferris.

07:00.690 --> 07:01.940
I need to test this.

07:18.210 --> 07:19.420
What just...?

07:31.220 --> 07:32.640
You mustn't.

07:33.140 --> 07:36.690
Master Subaru...
haven't you noticed?

07:36.690 --> 07:37.770
What?

07:45.740 --> 07:48.570
This won't stop me.

07:48.570 --> 07:51.200
You mustn't... Master Subaru...

07:51.200 --> 07:53.540
I cannot accept what you're trying to do.

07:53.540 --> 07:55.040
Come on, think about it!

07:55.040 --> 07:57.620
I'll be fine!
It just hurts a little.

07:57.620 --> 08:00.960
We have no guarantee
it'll stay that way.

08:00.960 --> 08:05.270
If both of us become incapacitated...

08:05.270 --> 08:06.760
...that would be fatal...

08:06.760 --> 08:07.550
But...

08:08.310 --> 08:10.930
You said it yourself,
Master Subaru...

08:11.460 --> 08:14.970
..."Leave the rest to me"...

08:16.020 --> 08:18.640
Please say it to me...

08:20.230 --> 08:24.280
..."Leave the rest to me"...

08:26.990 --> 08:28.110
Ms. Crusch.

08:28.110 --> 08:29.530
Don't worry.

08:29.530 --> 08:30.950
Please take your time and rest.

08:32.200 --> 08:34.410
Master... Subaru...

08:34.840 --> 08:38.370
You can leave the rest to me.

08:39.080 --> 08:40.080
Okay...

08:43.250 --> 08:44.960
Sorry, Ferris.

08:44.960 --> 08:46.550
I have to go.

08:46.550 --> 08:49.800
I... what should I do...?

08:49.800 --> 08:51.510
We need your strength.

08:52.070 --> 08:55.140
More people are going to get hurt
from here on out,

08:55.140 --> 08:58.810
and without you,
there'll be a lot we can't save.

08:58.810 --> 09:00.480
So please, I'm counting on you.

09:00.960 --> 09:04.480
I can't even save the one person
I want to save the most...

09:04.480 --> 09:05.650
Ferris...

09:05.650 --> 09:07.820
Sorry... That was dumb of me...

09:08.400 --> 09:11.410
Let me stay with her alone
a little longer...

09:16.330 --> 09:17.370
Thank you.

09:17.370 --> 09:20.750
Nah, if anything,
she's the one who motivated me.

09:25.340 --> 09:26.670
Sir Subaru.

09:26.670 --> 09:32.180
I have something to report
regarding the battle at the city hall.

09:32.180 --> 09:33.180
What is it?

09:33.640 --> 09:36.690
It is about those two cultists
guarding the Archbishop.

09:36.690 --> 09:39.180
The identities
of those two sword fighters.

09:39.770 --> 09:41.770
One of them is Eight-Arms Kurgan,

09:41.770 --> 09:44.810
the strongest swordsman
of the Vollachia Empire.

09:44.810 --> 09:48.190
He was an eight-armed greatsword wielder,

09:48.190 --> 09:51.240
who supposedly died over ten years ago.

09:51.240 --> 09:52.780
He's dead...?

09:52.780 --> 09:54.490
And the other is...

09:56.990 --> 10:00.580
The previous Sword Saint,
Theresia van Astrea.

10:00.580 --> 10:02.790
My wife, who should have fallen

10:02.790 --> 10:07.040
to the White Whale in the expedition
over fifteen years ago.

10:08.420 --> 10:11.170
During the Demi-Human War
a few decades ago,

10:11.170 --> 10:15.140
there was once someone who used
forbidden arts to control the dead.

10:15.140 --> 10:19.420
While that fiend has already perished,
the forbidden arts might have survived.

10:19.420 --> 10:21.270
And they're using it to raise the dead...

10:22.470 --> 10:26.690
These undead came
to be known as corpse soldiers.

10:26.690 --> 10:27.860
Corpse soldiers...?!

10:28.330 --> 10:31.820
Please keep it a secret from Reinhard.

10:36.280 --> 10:40.330
You mean you're not gonna
tell him about your wife?

10:40.830 --> 10:45.830
Sir Subaru, are you aware
that the Sword Saint Blessing is unique?

10:45.830 --> 10:48.420
Only that all the Sword Saints
in history had it,

10:48.420 --> 10:51.840
and that it made them really strong.

10:52.200 --> 10:54.720
At a surface level, yes, that is correct.

10:54.720 --> 10:59.430
However, there is one trait
that sets it apart from other blessings:

11:00.010 --> 11:02.810
It is inherited.

11:03.210 --> 11:05.130
What do you mean by "inherited"?

11:05.130 --> 11:08.270
This blessing has resided
within the Astrea family for generations,

11:08.750 --> 11:12.530
and the next Sword Saint
is always chosen from their bloodline.

11:12.530 --> 11:16.740
My wife's blessing, too,
was passed down to Reinhard.

11:16.740 --> 11:18.990
A blessing inherited through blood...

11:18.990 --> 11:21.990
So Reinhard got it
after your wife passed away?

11:22.700 --> 11:25.960
He inherited it in the middle of
the battle with the White Whale.

11:27.630 --> 11:30.210
My wife lost her blessing during the fight

11:30.670 --> 11:34.380
and became an ordinary woman, who had to
defend her allies as the rear guard.

11:35.010 --> 11:39.220
The man who stole the sword from her
was none other than me.

11:39.220 --> 11:42.140
I made the Sword God's favorite
throw away her sword,

11:42.140 --> 11:44.390
and that was what invited her doom.

11:44.820 --> 11:46.390
Mr. Wilhelm...

11:46.390 --> 11:49.980
It is a fact that I berated Reinhard
for inheriting the blessing.

11:50.470 --> 11:52.360
He was but a grieving boy

11:52.360 --> 11:55.990
burdened with a heavy fate
right after losing his grandmother.

11:55.990 --> 11:58.490
Yet I couldn't forgive him.

11:58.490 --> 12:00.070
I regret it deeply.

12:00.620 --> 12:05.370
Reinhard was never to blame
for my wife's death.

12:05.370 --> 12:07.960
Even if I keep quiet
about the corpse soldiers,

12:07.960 --> 12:10.460
we can't predict
when they'll show up next.

12:10.460 --> 12:13.920
Your worry is completely unfounded.

12:14.630 --> 12:20.600
There is no way my wife,
Theresia, wouldn't come to see me.

12:22.720 --> 12:24.470
And you're actually not kiddin' me?

12:24.470 --> 12:26.480
Do not make me repeat myself.

12:27.100 --> 12:30.850
I shall make for District 4
and lop off Wrath's head for you.

12:30.850 --> 12:33.400
The diva shall accompany me, of course.

12:33.400 --> 12:34.690
Hey, wait up!

12:34.690 --> 12:37.490
Why in the world would you pick me?!

12:37.490 --> 12:40.490
Remember how much your singing

12:40.490 --> 12:44.160
moved the vulgar masses' hearts
as we were going around the shelters?

12:44.160 --> 12:46.410
You need simply repeat that.

12:46.410 --> 12:47.750
Wouldn't you agree, peasant?

12:48.190 --> 12:51.250
Right. Her stupidity and singing voice

12:51.250 --> 12:54.420
might be the perfect counter
for Wrath's Authority.

12:54.420 --> 12:56.210
But there's no guarantee.

12:56.210 --> 12:57.840
A guarantee, you say?

12:57.840 --> 13:00.130
Any ideas on how we can check?

13:06.890 --> 13:08.350
I've been blessed just now.

13:08.350 --> 13:09.850
Blessed with what? A child?

13:09.850 --> 13:11.520
The Blessing of Judgment.

13:11.930 --> 13:15.570
It lets me analyze
other people's blessings.

13:19.110 --> 13:20.780
This is surprising.

13:20.780 --> 13:24.200
She bears the Blessing of Telepathy.

13:24.200 --> 13:27.200
I never thought
it could be used for singing.

13:27.200 --> 13:29.160
I'm more surprised at you!

13:29.160 --> 13:30.830
You got blessed "just now"?

13:30.830 --> 13:33.170
It's easier said than done...

13:33.170 --> 13:37.380
I'm not really sure...
if I can answer your expectations...

13:37.380 --> 13:39.170
I see.

13:39.170 --> 13:44.510
So you do not believe in the songs
you've inherited from your predecessors.

13:44.510 --> 13:46.430
And what exactly do you mean by that?

13:46.430 --> 13:50.060
You've faithfully sung the song
of your ancestors to the present,

13:50.060 --> 13:52.600
yet you fall silent
and shrink back in fear

13:52.600 --> 13:54.980
when the people's hearts
cry out for salvation.

13:54.980 --> 13:57.440
I have no need for crying mutts—

13:59.320 --> 14:00.820
Now you've said it!

14:00.820 --> 14:02.990
Yep, you just said it!

14:02.990 --> 14:05.910
Fine, I'll do it! Bring it on!

14:05.910 --> 14:07.870
I'll show you what singing really is!

14:07.870 --> 14:10.390
I can't call myself a proud woman
if I stay silent now!

14:10.950 --> 14:13.000
I wanted to sing a requiem
for Mr. Kiritaka

14:13.000 --> 14:16.210
as this city's waters tragically
claim his lifeless body,

14:16.210 --> 14:17.670
but no, I shall not!

14:17.670 --> 14:21.130
You can count on me,
for I am none other than Liliana!

14:21.130 --> 14:24.760
Okay, so we'll leave Wrath
to Priscilla and Liliana.

14:24.760 --> 14:25.640
Any objections?

14:26.060 --> 14:28.720
Well, you've convinced me.

14:28.720 --> 14:30.850
Anyone here disagree?

14:31.210 --> 14:34.480
Okay, next is Lust in District 1.

14:34.480 --> 14:37.190
There will probably be more
enemies there than anywhere else.

14:37.190 --> 14:38.820
The Archbishop herself,

14:38.820 --> 14:42.240
those two cultists,
and maybe even demibeasts too.

14:42.630 --> 14:47.030
You're saying
they're all Lust's personal forces?

14:47.030 --> 14:50.870
From what I've seen,
I'm pretty sure they're connected to Lust.

14:50.870 --> 14:52.000
As for the two cultists—

14:52.000 --> 14:56.960
They are likely corpse soldiers
controlled through forbidden arts.

14:56.960 --> 15:00.920
You're saying they're swordsmen
who were brought back from the dead?

15:00.920 --> 15:04.590
That means I was dukin' it out
with Eight-Arms Kurgan himself.

15:04.590 --> 15:08.140
A guy that strong with eight arms...

15:08.140 --> 15:10.010
There ain't no one else it could be!

15:10.010 --> 15:13.600
And that woman's gotta be someone
on the same level as him!

15:13.600 --> 15:17.230
A forbidden art that desecrates the dead
and turns them into corpse soldiers...

15:17.230 --> 15:21.570
Yes, it does match Lust's twisted tastes.

15:21.570 --> 15:23.190
The logic is sound.

15:23.630 --> 15:28.910
Yeah, and I want to let Mr. Wilhelm
and Garfiel handle Lust.

15:28.910 --> 15:30.330
Ch-Chief?!

15:30.760 --> 15:33.910
Aren't we goin'
to save Lady Emilia, Chief?!

15:33.910 --> 15:35.500
Ya gotta take me with you—

15:35.500 --> 15:39.500
I'm happy you'd say that.
Encouraged, even.

15:39.850 --> 15:44.880
But you have your own scores
to settle, remember?

15:49.220 --> 15:54.100
Lady Crusch is currently suffering
from Lust's curse.

15:54.100 --> 15:57.520
Please allow me to avenge my liege—

15:57.520 --> 15:58.600
I object.

15:58.600 --> 16:00.230
Reinhard...

16:00.230 --> 16:03.190
You are not calm right now, Grandfather.

16:03.190 --> 16:05.490
I should be the one to handle them.

16:05.490 --> 16:09.870
Reinhard, have you forgotten
who your grandfather is?

16:09.870 --> 16:11.450
However, Grandfather—

16:11.450 --> 16:13.620
I am the man hailed as the Sword Demon.

16:13.620 --> 16:17.960
Being anything but calm
is a given for me on the battlefield.

16:18.480 --> 16:21.670
Having persisted for fourteen years,

16:21.670 --> 16:25.080
my rusted blade was still sharp enough
to cut down my wife's killer.

16:25.080 --> 16:27.550
It is still too soon for it
to remain sheathed forever.

16:28.550 --> 16:29.590
Sir Subaru.

16:30.440 --> 16:33.220
Please take Reinhard
with you in your upcoming battle.

16:33.850 --> 16:37.680
Besides, I was just about to get to that.

16:38.110 --> 16:42.190
I want you to join me
in the fight against Greed.

16:42.190 --> 16:47.370
He's invincible, so we're gonna need
the strongest guy here to beat him.

16:48.200 --> 16:53.120
I'm askin' ya too!
Please, help the Chief and Lady Emilia!

16:54.660 --> 16:56.200
Then give me your word.

16:56.700 --> 17:00.960
Just as you have expectations of me,
I'll hold you to mine as well.

17:00.960 --> 17:03.190
Let's both see our objectives through.

17:04.170 --> 17:05.880
Yeah! Leave it to me!

17:05.880 --> 17:08.880
I will place my trust in you
and Grandfather,

17:08.880 --> 17:10.590
and I will become Subaru's blade.

17:14.510 --> 17:17.180
Sorry for always relying on you.

17:17.180 --> 17:21.600
I'll find a way to make up for the things
you can't do, so you can count on me.

17:22.980 --> 17:23.880
What?

17:25.360 --> 17:28.280
That's probably no big deal for you.

17:28.680 --> 17:31.240
Yes, of course.

17:31.240 --> 17:35.660
I'll leave the things
I can't handle to you.

17:35.660 --> 17:36.990
Huh? Yeah!

17:36.990 --> 17:41.080
Feel free to get your hopes up,
'cause I've got high hopes for you!

17:42.790 --> 17:46.380
Lastly, for Gluttony...

17:46.380 --> 17:47.400
Yes,

17:48.130 --> 17:50.840
leave Gluttony to Ricardo and me.

17:50.840 --> 17:52.510
Why're ya the one callin' the shots?

17:52.510 --> 17:54.800
- I'm in, though.
- I'm countin' on you.

17:55.200 --> 17:58.390
Ferris and I are gonna
stay behind at the city hall.

17:58.390 --> 17:59.640
Everythin' good?

17:59.640 --> 18:01.810
Alright, let's do this!

18:01.810 --> 18:03.060
We'll fight!

18:06.060 --> 18:08.530
And we'll win!

18:13.200 --> 18:14.450
Well, this is a surprise!

18:14.820 --> 18:16.950
You looked lovely in your previous attire,

18:16.950 --> 18:19.290
but now, you are simply sublime!

18:19.720 --> 18:23.500
We are truly the most fitting
couple in the world!

18:23.960 --> 18:29.130
Looking at you, I was right
to leave the seat of #79 open!

18:29.130 --> 18:31.470
Why did you specifically
leave that number open?

18:31.470 --> 18:32.880
Well, you see...

18:32.880 --> 18:37.220
There was another woman I previously
sought worthy of that number.

18:37.560 --> 18:38.950
Sadly, before we were wed,

18:38.950 --> 18:41.930
I deemed her unworthy,
hence the empty seat.

18:41.930 --> 18:44.480
But thanks to that, I met you.

18:44.480 --> 18:47.140
We truly are bound by fate!

18:47.730 --> 18:49.690
Another woman and an empty seat...

18:49.690 --> 18:53.490
Now, let us exchange our vows.

18:53.490 --> 18:54.650
Hey, Regulus.

18:55.110 --> 18:59.120
There are a few things I'd like you
to tell me before the ceremony.

19:01.870 --> 19:06.080
I actually had a few things
I wanted to tell you, too.

19:06.460 --> 19:11.210
Don't fret, these are only natural
for every wife to follow.

19:12.090 --> 19:13.670
First...

19:14.800 --> 19:18.890
You are forbidden to smile
once we are married.

19:19.390 --> 19:20.390
Huh?

19:20.390 --> 19:22.890
Yours is already a sweet and lovely face.

19:22.890 --> 19:25.770
Why would you ruin it with a smile?

19:25.770 --> 19:29.110
It is simply unforgivable, you see!

19:29.110 --> 19:33.110
As such, I forbid you to express
emotion altogether.

19:34.120 --> 19:37.610
You shall not laugh,
cry, rage, nor rejoice!

19:37.610 --> 19:39.890
Your sole duty is to look adorable.

19:40.910 --> 19:42.120
That was really unplea—

19:42.540 --> 19:43.660
Now listen here!

19:43.660 --> 19:47.750
Do you perhaps have some
sort of complaint with me?

19:47.750 --> 19:50.880
I have done nothing
but make compromises for your sake,

19:50.880 --> 19:53.710
yet you can't even appreciate it.

19:53.710 --> 19:57.970
In other words,
you are belittling me as an individual!

19:57.970 --> 20:00.760
This is an infringement of my rights!

20:00.760 --> 20:02.680
That is not something I can forgive...!

20:03.110 --> 20:04.180
You know,

20:04.180 --> 20:07.770
I think marriage is a really happy thing.

20:09.850 --> 20:11.190
It's a ceremony

20:11.190 --> 20:14.530
that gives shape to the thoughts
of people who love each other.

20:14.530 --> 20:17.860
It happens when you find
that one special person

20:17.860 --> 20:20.840
among the countless people in the world,
and they love you back.

20:20.840 --> 20:23.620
I think that's really incredible.

20:24.200 --> 20:28.960
So, Regulus, why do you refer
to your wives as numbers?

20:28.960 --> 20:31.380
Are you that fixated on names?

20:31.380 --> 20:34.550
You would obsess so much
over superficial things?

20:34.550 --> 20:36.920
That's rather shallow, don't you think?

20:36.920 --> 20:41.890
But Subaru calls me Emilia-tan,
and I don't dislike it.

20:41.890 --> 20:43.600
..."Subaru"?

20:44.090 --> 20:48.810
When Subaru calls me "Emilia-tan,"
his voice is so full of feelings.

20:48.810 --> 20:51.230
And when he just calls me
"Emilia" sometimes,

20:51.230 --> 20:53.650
it's always obvious it's a special moment.

20:53.650 --> 20:56.360
There's no way that's meaningless.

20:56.360 --> 20:59.740
A name should have thought behind it.

20:59.740 --> 21:00.780
Now listen here.

21:00.780 --> 21:02.700
Who exactly is this "Subaru"?

21:02.700 --> 21:05.080
It's a man, isn't it?

21:05.080 --> 21:07.660
What kind of bride brings up
another man's name

21:07.660 --> 21:12.460
in front of her groom,
just moments before their wedding?

21:12.460 --> 21:15.170
Do you even have a lick of common sense?

21:15.170 --> 21:17.840
Even if he was someone
you hardly interacted with,

21:17.840 --> 21:19.630
it would still be hurtful to me, yes?

21:19.630 --> 21:22.260
He isn't someone I hardly interacted with!

21:22.260 --> 21:25.220
Subaru is my one and only knight.

21:25.220 --> 21:28.350
He calls me by my name
and tells me he loves me!

21:31.560 --> 21:32.770
Don't you dare move!

21:32.770 --> 21:36.150
If you do, I'll eradicate everything
below her head!

21:36.690 --> 21:38.190
I will hear your explanation.

21:38.190 --> 21:43.160
Choose your words carefully to ensure
there are no misunderstandings.

21:43.160 --> 21:47.370
I have no intention of turning
this wedding into someone's funeral.

21:47.370 --> 21:50.960
You see what I'm getting at, right?

21:51.480 --> 21:55.670
Marriage is for lovers,
like when a man and a woman love each other.

21:55.670 --> 21:58.660
But I'm not yet qualified for that.

21:59.300 --> 22:00.130
After all,

22:00.130 --> 22:04.180
I still don't know what it's like
to love a man as a woman.

22:04.180 --> 22:08.680
So when Subaru tells me he loves me,

22:08.680 --> 22:13.270
I can't give him the answer he wants...
or the other one, either.

22:13.670 --> 22:18.690
I know it's horrible of me to do that,
and that it's hurtful and bothersome.

22:18.690 --> 22:22.950
Still, even though I've never fallen
in love with someone before,

22:22.950 --> 22:25.700
I know I'll fall in love
with someone one day.

22:25.700 --> 22:29.330
I will love someone as a woman.

22:29.330 --> 22:33.830
And when that happens,
I already know who it'll be.

22:33.830 --> 22:35.250
So...

22:35.250 --> 22:38.130
I will never be yours.

22:39.590 --> 22:40.960
Is that so?!

22:40.960 --> 22:47.420
I no longer have any interest in marrying
an impure adulterer like you!

22:47.420 --> 22:48.850
What a relief!

22:53.770 --> 22:54.940
Seriously?!

22:54.940 --> 22:57.860
Did we really kick the door
at the same time?

22:57.860 --> 22:59.460
The heck are those legs made of?!

22:59.460 --> 23:01.820
Apologies. I failed to hold back.

23:01.820 --> 23:04.780
You just put a dent in my coolness, man!

23:06.240 --> 23:11.080
You've got some nerve barging
into a sacred wedding.

23:11.080 --> 23:15.120
I don't remember inviting any men here.

23:15.120 --> 23:17.420
Who are you and where did you come from?

23:17.420 --> 23:20.050
What gifts have you brought me, hm?

23:20.050 --> 23:23.130
I'm a spirit knight
whose partner spirit is absent,

23:23.130 --> 23:24.510
Natsuki Subaru!

23:24.510 --> 23:26.510
Hailing from the Sword Saint family,

23:26.510 --> 23:28.720
Reinhard van Astrea!

23:30.430 --> 23:33.770
We're here to object to this wedding!

23:35.020 --> 23:35.770
THE PERSON I'LL FALL FOR SOMEDAY

23:35.770 --> 23:39.320
THE PERSON I'LL FALL FOR SOMEDAY
I'll be taking your bride now!

23:39.320 --> 23:40.020
THE PERSON I'LL FALL FOR SOMEDAY
